 challenging move. It immediately tests Black’s center, opens lines for White’s bishops, and could lead to a strong initiative. Since White is better developed, opening the position is favorable. Other moves like Bf1-c4 or Nf3-g5 are less forcing and give Black time to consolidate.\n\nAnswer: P: d4-d5"}
